#: ../../../platform_support.md:3
msgid "Platform Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:5
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc's targets differ in how complete they are. This page describes the "
"status of each. {doc}`arch_support` lists the architectures that are tested "
"continuously, and {ref}`porting` describes what a target needs in order to "
"be added or kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:10
msgid "Used in production"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:12
msgid ""
"These targets have, or are expected to soon have, users deploying LLVM-libc "
"in a production environment. They are given some amount of priority over the "
"more experimental targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Operating system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Architectures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Baremetal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "AArch64, RISC-V, 32-bit Arm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:21
msgid ""
"New functionality should be enabled on all platforms when possible, but may "
"be rolled out to just these targets first as the primary development "
"targets. See {ref}`code_organization`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:25
msgid "Other targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:27
msgid ""
"The remaining targets are partially complete or experimental. Breakage on "
"them is still a bug, but contributors are not expected to be able to test "
"them."
msgstr ""

