msgid "GPU (AMDGPU, NVPTX)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Maintained by the GPU maintainers. See {doc}`the GPU docs <gpu/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Baremetal Hexagon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Newer target (as of 2026) but hopefully an area of growth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "FreeBSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "A port is in progress. It has a maintainer and presubmit CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "macOS and Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid ""
"Overlay mode only. The overlay tests run in presubmit, but both ports need "
"significant work, and a full build for these systems has not been designed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Linux on 32-bit Arm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid ""
"Primarily used to test the 32-bit Arm code that the baremetal target also "
"uses, alongside the baremetal Arm tests that are being rolled out in CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Linux on PowerPC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid ""
"Minimal. It exists mainly so that the code shared with libc++ keeps building "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Linux on i386"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid ""
"Theoretically [in the works](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/"
"93709), though it may be sunset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "UEFI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:0
msgid "Experimental and incomplete. See {doc}`the UEFI docs <uefi/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:41
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc is also being integrated into the Android and Fuchsia operating "
"systems via {doc}`overlay mode <overlay_mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:44
msgid "Breakages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:46
msgid ""
"A change that breaks any buildbot should be reverted or, if the fix is "
"trivial, fixed forward. This is intended to follow LLVM's [patch reversion "
"policy](https://llvm.org/docs/DeveloperPolicy.html#patch-reversion-policy)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:50
msgid "Operating system versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:52
msgid ""
"For Linux, we support kernel versions as listed on [kernel.org](https://"
"kernel.org/), including `longterm` (not past EOL date), `stable`, and "
"`mainline` versions. We actively adopt new features from `linux-next`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:57
msgid ""
"For Windows, we plan to support products within their lifecycle. Please "
"refer to [Search Product and Services Lifecycle Information](https://"
"learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/products/?products=windows) for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platform_support.md:60
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc does not guarantee backward compatibility with operating systems "
"that have reached their EOL. Compatibility patches for obsolete operating "
"systems will not be accepted."
msgstr ""
